.* --- option 5 on a connection
:PANEL NAME=DSPCNN HELP=HLPCNN5 KEYL=CNN5KEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM BOTSEP=NONE.Display TCP Connection Status
:DATA DEPTH='*' SCROLL=IND.
:DATACOL WIDTH=49.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.Connection identification
:DATAI VAR=DRHOST USAGE=OUTPUT.Remote host name
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI VAR=DRADR USAGE=OUTPUT.Remote internet address
:DATAI VAR=DRPORT USAGE=OUTPUT.Remote port
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAI VAR=DLHOST USAGE=OUTPUT.Local host name
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI VAR=DLADR USAGE=OUTPUT.Local internet address
:DATAI VAR=DLPORT USAGE=OUTPUT.Local port
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAI VAR=DUSER USAGE=OUTPUT.Associated user profile
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.TCP programming interface information
:DATAI VAR=DSTATE USAGE=OUTPUT.State
:DATAI VAR=DOPEN USAGE=OUTPUT.Connection open type
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.Timing information
:DATAI VAR=DIDLE USAGE=OUTPUT.Idle time
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI VAR=DLAST USAGE=OUTPUT.Last activity date/time
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAI VAR=DRTT USAGE=OUTPUT.Round-trip time
:DATAI VAR=DRTTV USAGE=OUTPUT.Round-trip variance
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAC.
:DATAI VAR=DBOUT USAGE=OUTPUT.Bytes out
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI VAR=DOBUF USAGE=OUTPUT.Outgoing bytes buffered
:DATAI VAR=DUSNDNXT USAGE=OUTPUT.User send next
:DATAI VAR=DSNDNXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Send next
:DATAI VAR=DSNDUNA USAGE=OUTPUT.Send unacknowledged
:DATAI VAR=DOPUSH USAGE=OUTPUT.Outgoing push number
:DATAI VAR=DOURG USAGE=OUTPUT.Outgoing urgency number
:DATAI VAR=DOWIN USAGE=OUTPUT.Outgoing window number
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAI VAR=DBIN USAGE=OUTPUT.Bytes in
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI VAR=DIBUF USAGE=OUTPUT.Incoming bytes buffered
:DATAI VAR=DRCVNXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Receive next
:DATAI VAR=DURCVNXT USAGE=OUTPUT.User receive next
:DATAI VAR=DIPUSH USAGE=OUTPUT.Incoming push number
:DATAI VAR=DIURG USAGE=OUTPUT.Incoming urgency number
:DATAI VAR=DIWIN USAGE=OUTPUT.Incoming window number
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.Retransmission information
:DATAI VAR=DRETR USAGE=OUTPUT.Total retransmissions
:DATAI VAR=DCRETR USAGE=OUTPUT.Current retransmissions
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.Send window information
:DATAI VAR=DSWMAX USAGE=OUTPUT.Maximum size
:DATAI VAR=DSWCUR USAGE=OUTPUT.Current size
:DATAI VAR=DSWUPD USAGE=OUTPUT.Last update
:DATAI VAR=DSWACK USAGE=OUTPUT.Last update acknowledged
:DATAI VAR=DCWND USAGE=OUTPUT.Congestion window
:DATAI VAR=DSSTH USAGE=OUTPUT.Slow start threshold
:DATAI VAR=DMSS USAGE=OUTPUT.Maximum segment size
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.Precedence and security
:DATAI VAR=DPREC USAGE=OUTPUT.Precedence
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.Initialization information
:DATAI VAR=DISS USAGE=OUTPUT.Initial send sequence number
:DATAI VAR=DIRS USAGE=OUTPUT.Initial receive sequence number
:EDATAGRP.
:EDATA.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
.* --- option 8 on a connection
:PANEL NAME=DSPJOBS HELP=HLPJOBS KEYL=JOBKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM BOTSEP=NONE.Display Jobs Using Connection
:DATA DEPTH=7.
:DATACOL WIDTH=30.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=JCTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Connection type
:DATAI VAR=JLADR USAGE=OUTPUT.Local address
:DATAI VAR=JLPORT USAGE=OUTPUT.Local port
:DATAI VAR=JRADR USAGE=OUTPUT.Remote address
:DATAI VAR=JRPORT USAGE=OUTPUT.Remote port
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Type options, press Enter.
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=JOBS SCROLL=YES MAXHEAD=2.(No jobs)
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&JNBR./&JUSER./&JNAME.)'.5=Work with job
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=JPAD USAGE=OUTPUT.
:LISTCOL VAR=JNAME USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=13.Name
:LISTCOL VAR=JUSER USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=13.User
:LISTCOL VAR=JNBR USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=9.Number
:LISTCOL VAR=JTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=8.Type
:LISTCOL VAR=JCUR USAGE=OUTPUT.Current User
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
.* --- option 10
:PANEL NAME=DSPSTS HELP=HLPSTS KEYL=STSKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Display TCP/IP Stack Status
:DATA DEPTH='*' SCROLL=IND.
:DATACOL WIDTH=45.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=S4 USAGE=OUTPUT.IPv4 stack status
:DATAI VAR=S6 USAGE=OUTPUT.IPv6 stack status
:DATAI VAR=SLMT USAGE=OUTPUT.Limited mode
:DATAI VAR=SACT USAGE=OUTPUT.How long active
:DATAI VAR=SSTR USAGE=OUTPUT.When last started
:DATAI VAR=SEND USAGE=OUTPUT.When last ended
:DATAI VAR=SWSJ USAGE=OUTPUT.Who last started - job name
:DATAI VAR=SWSU USAGE=OUTPUT.Who last started - job user
:DATAI VAR=SWSN USAGE=OUTPUT.Who last started - job number
:DATAI VAR=SWEJ USAGE=OUTPUT.Who last ended - job name
:DATAI VAR=SWEU USAGE=OUTPUT.Who last ended - job user
:DATAI VAR=SWEN USAGE=OUTPUT.Who last ended - job number
:EDATA.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
.* --- help
:HELP NAME=HLPMENU.Work with TCP/IP Network Status - Help
:P.What the network is doing now: the interfaces and whether they are up,
the routes the system uses, every connection and listening port with the
job that holds it, for IPv4 and IPv6, and the state of the stack.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPIFC.Interface Status - Help
:P.Each interface with its network and the line it runs on. F11 shows
the virtual LAN of the line instead of the status. Option 5 shows an
interface's details, 8 the routes that leave through it, 12 the line's
status; with the authority to change configuration, 9 starts and 10 ends
an interface.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPIFC5.Display TCP/IP Interface Status - Help
:P.One interface: its address with the network and host parts, the line
under it and the values it was configured with.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPRTE.Route Information - Help
:P.The routes the system uses now, the default route last. F11 shows
each route's type of service, MTU, type and where it came from.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPRTE5.Route Details - Help
:P.One route and the values it is used with.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPCNN.Connection Status - Help
:P.Every TCP connection and listening socket, and every UDP socket, with
the remote end, the local port, how long it has been idle and its state.
F11 shows the bytes it moved and the user that holds it, then the
addresses and port numbers. Option 5 shows the details, 8 the jobs that
hold it; with the authority to change configuration, 4 ends it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPCNN5.Display Connection Status - Help
:P.One connection: both ends, its state, its timers and the bytes it has
moved.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPJOBS.Display Jobs Using Connection - Help
:P.The jobs whose processes hold the connection's socket.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPSTS.Display TCP/IP Stack Status - Help
:P.Whether IPv4 and IPv6 are up, since when, and which job started or
ended TCP/IP last.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
